Subject: [qnx-porter 0001] main-stack
Source: deterministic rule
Reason: Crash on QNX: cJSON_Duplicate_rec() calls itself until the stack runs out (the backtrace is cJSON_Duplicate_rec <- cJSON_Duplicate_rec <- ...). A QNX main thread gets about 464 KiB of stack unless the program is linked with qcc -N; a Linux one usually has 8 MiB. Every program is now linked with -N8M, which writes an 8 MiB stack size into its QNX ELF note.
Error: Memory fault (SIGSEGV) in cJSON_Duplicate_rec, deep recursion
---
--- a/qnx-toolchain.cmake
+++ b/qnx-toolchain.cmake
@@ -15,8 +15,8 @@
 # -g: debug info only (same code), so a crash on the target gives file:line in its backtrace
 set(CMAKE_C_FLAGS_INIT "-g ")
 set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_INIT "-g ")
-set(CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS_INIT "-L/home/chirag/qnx-porter/ports/cJSON/work/stubs")
-set(CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS_INIT "-L/home/chirag/qnx-porter/ports/cJSON/work/stubs")
+set(CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS_INIT "-L/home/chirag/qnx-porter/ports/cJSON/work/stubs -N8M")
+set(CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS_INIT "-L/home/chirag/qnx-porter/ports/cJSON/work/stubs -N8M")
 # Flags after the project's own (appended by the compiler wrappers in -): none
 # Libraries the agent adds go at the end of every link line, after the objects that need them.
 set(CMAKE_C_STANDARD_LIBRARIES "")
